                <pb facs="0188" n="82" xml:id="pg82"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pacheco to Mr.
                            Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States in Guatemala and
                                Honduras</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-09-29"><hi rendition="#italic">September 29,
                            1891</hi>.</date> (Received October 17.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 73.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your instruction No. 21, of August 22, and to report that I have addressed a
                    communication to the minister of foreign relations on the subject of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Colima</hi> arms, strictly in accordance with your
                    instructions.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">R. Pacheco</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
